PRETABLE block -- m88kexcdeliver (#502) TABLE 12, THE DISCRIMINATING TABLE.  Written BEFORE any mutant is built.
2026-09-06 ~16:0x.  Corrections go to PRETABLE12_ADDENDUM*.out; this file's mtime is the order proof.

WHY THIS TABLE EXISTS: A PANEL DISAGREEMENT THAT A VOTE CANNOT SETTLE.
Pass 8 split three ways on one question -- does a status-bit conjunct on the SFRZ re-route's TRAP side escape the
shipped 46-row detector?

  codex (GPT-6 Astra, max)  ONE MORE REPAIR: `if (!is_trap || !(PSR & IND))' is predicted 46/46, because all eleven
                            trapfrozen rows enter with PSR 0x8000000b so the added disjunct is false for every one of
                            them, and errind cannot see it because `!is_trap' is already true there.  NOT BUILT.
  grok (4.6, xhigh)         THE SAME CLASS, found independently, with four edits and four rows named.  NOT BUILT.
  kimi (3)                  GO-WITH-CHANGES: four families enumerated, "killable-and-undisclosed survivors: ZERO".
                            Its re-route family reads `{label trap x 11, diagnostic both ways}' -- it counts the trap
                            side as covered BY the eleven trapfrozen rows.
  opus5                     Measured THREE sweeps at 46/46 -- but at the SWITCH-1 ARMS, a DIFFERENT SITE.  So the
                            "zero survivors" claim is already refuted in general; the RE-ROUTE cell specifically is
                            still unmeasured, and that is the cell codex and grok named.

This project settles disagreements by measurement, never by tally.  Three seats predicting is not evidence.

THE MUTANTS (exact edits, all on the re-route's INNER condition; anchor `\t\tif (!is_trap) {`).
  M_RRTRAPIND   `if (!is_trap || !(cpu->cd.m88k.cr[M88K_CR_PSR] & M88K_PSR_IND)) {`
                PREDICTED 46/46 (codex, grok).  Reason to believe it: every trapfrozen row reaches the re-route with
                PSR 0x8000000b -- MODE|SFD1|IND|SFRZ -- read off killtable11/BASE.out, not assumed, so `!(PSR & IND)'
                is FALSE at all eleven and the mutant is behaviourally identical to the fix on them.  errind and errc
                are `!is_trap' rows, where the first disjunct already decides.
  M_RRTRAPC     `if (!is_trap || (cpu->cd.m88k.cr[M88K_CR_PSR] & M88K_PSR_C)) {`
                PREDICTED 46/46.  Same reason, opposite bit: C is CLEAR in 0x8000000b, so the disjunct is false at all
                eleven.  Built because one cell is an instance and two are a class.
  CTL_RRTRAPINV `if (!is_trap || (cpu->cd.m88k.cr[M88K_CR_PSR] & M88K_PSR_IND)) {`   -- THE POLARITY TWIN, A CONTROL.
                PREDICTED HEAVILY RED.  IND is SET at all eleven trapfrozen rows, so this re-routes EVERY frozen trap
                to ERROR: each should read STOP (entry 0x50 instead of its own vector) and bad=refatal (the re-route's
                diagnostic printed where the exemption should hold).  **This is what makes the other two results
                mean something.**  A mutant that will not die has three explanations and one of them is `the edit is
                mis-built'; the twin rules that out, because it is the same edit with one token changed.

WHAT EACH OUTCOME SETTLES, WRITTEN BEFORE THE RUN SO NEITHER RESULT CAN BE FITTED AFTERWARDS:
  * M_RRTRAPIND 46/46 AND CTL_RRTRAPINV heavily red  ->  codex and grok are RIGHT, kimi's "zero survivors" is refuted
    at this site as well as at the switch-1 arms, and the round owes the {is_trap} x {PSR bit} cells as part of the
    class closure Opus already specified for the arms.  L2, in-round.
  * M_RRTRAPIND RED  ->  codex and grok are WRONG and kimi is RIGHT about this cell; the eleven trapfrozen rows do
    cover the trap side, and the pass-8 record must say so and name which row caught it.
  * BOTH GREEN (mutant AND twin)  ->  the edit did not land, or the probe cannot see this site at all.  NOT a result.
    Check the find-text applied (the driver treats MUTANT-TEXT-NOT-FOUND as a failure) and check that BASE is 46/46.

CHANNEL, per the fourth pre-table check.  Under M_RRTRAPIND a trapfrozen row that WOULD have been exempted is instead
re-routed: its entry moves from 8*vector to 0x50 (RESULT STOP, since the breakpoint is set at the expected entry) and
the re-route's `[ SFRZ already set in PSR => ERROR ]' line appears where REFATAL_EXPECT says it must not (bad=refatal).
Both channels vary and the probe already reads both -- so if the mutant scores 46/46 it is because NO ROW REACHES THE
CELL, not because the oracle is blind.

APPARATUS, and the traps this round has already paid for:
  * Scratch clone /tmp/gxm88kexc_kill, verified cmp-clean against SEC with no sentinel before the table starts.
    Nothing writes to GXEMUL-SEC, build/, build-asan/, est/ or /tmp/gxsec-build.
  * The frozen instrument is the SHIPPED probe (v15, md5 eb11ab7c), copied into the table directory -- so the table
    measures what the gate runs, which is the records gap kimi named in its own pass-8 answer.
  * Sentinel per mutant; restore by re-copying from SEC, `cmp`, and REBUILD, with `[ binary -nt source ]` checked --
    a restore is not finished until the binary is rebuilt.
  * The driver is run from a FROZEN COPY so the original stays editable while it runs.
  * BASE is run before and after; if the closing BASE is not 46/46 the table is void whatever the mutants said.

PREDICTED TABLE:  BASE 46/46 -> M_RRTRAPIND 46/46 -> M_RRTRAPC 46/46 -> CTL_RRTRAPINV heavily red -> BASE_final 46/46.
